Following the end-to-end validation of "path A" on the Python side
(load extracted IT sub1 -> TLS handshake -> AppData round-trip), this
commit brings the bootstrap of the libfprint port for the VeriMark IT
to the driver source tree. The DT-side helpers (crypto, Synaptics KDF,
session management) are reusable as-is; only the USB transport and a
few constants differ between the DT and the IT.

proto.h/c:
- IT-specific protocol constants verbatim from the documented device trace
  (4-opcode init dance, plaintext TLS close_notify, 44 00 00 00 prefix
  for handshake records, firmware error sentinels 0x044f / 0x0406).
- IT USB topology (EP01 OUT, EP81 IN, EP83 INTR, MI_00).
- Pair frame sizes (401 B OUT, 802 B IN).

transport.h/c:
- New verimark_bulk_out / verimark_bulk_in primitives (libgusb-
  backed), mirroring the existing ctrl_out / ctrl_in helpers.
- Stubs for the no-libgusb standalone build.
- verimark_bulk_in implements the Python bulk_read_all loop: keeps
  reading chunks until a short packet (< 64 B) or a timeout, returns
  the total bytes received.

tests/test_it_proto.c — 10/10 green:
- VID/PID/EPs (047d:8054, EP01/81/83, MI_00).
- Pair opcode and sizes (0x93 / 401 B / 802 B).
- Error sentinels (0x044f not_allowed, 0x0406 invalid_arg).
- Init dance bytes verbatim (frames 4110 / 4114 / 4118 / 4122).
- TLS close_notify plaintext and Synaptics HS prefix.

All 12 tests are green (existing DT proto/crypto/tls/pairing/session/
handshake/storage/capture/match/enroll/bootstrap, plus the new IT
proto). No regression on the DT path.

Next steps (future sessions):
- High-level helper verimark_init_dance_it that sends the 4 opcodes
  and handles the close_notify recovery when the firmware-side
  session is stale.
- IT variant of the TLS handshake (5-cipher ClientHello, otherwise
  identical to the DT path).
- Wiring inside open(): replace the current introspection-only stub
  with the full IT path (init dance -> handshake -> session_active).
